## 1. Introduction

Scripts (or uuScripts) are a powerful way to automate tasks and extend the functionality of the system. The scripts
are basically dynamically loaded JavaScript files that are executed asynchronously in uuScriptEngine subApp.
The subApp uuScriptEngine handles inputs, outputs, and the execution of the script. The business logic is then
handled by the provided script. The script is executed in a sandboxed environment, which means that it has limited access to the
system and cannot perform any actions that could compromise the security of the system. By default, the script has
a single executable function, which is called when the script is executed. The script can also require other scripts
via a function called uuScriptRequire.

For detailed guidelines, see [script-engine.md](mdc:docs/script/script-engine.md).
Always follow the examples and templates in the provided guideline, especially for the most common tasks (validation,
error handling, helpers, uuAppClient, uuUri...).

