## 3. Script Structure

- Every script must contain a single async function main, which is executed at the bottom of the file.
- Every script must contain a section separated by comments, even if that would mean empty section. The sections are as follow:
-- imports
-- names
-- mockups
-- errors
-- validateDtoIn
-- helpers
-- main

For detailed guidelines, see [script-engine.md](mdc:docs/script/script-engine.md).

## 4. API Specifications for AppClient

Main usage of uuScript is to provide a way to use uuAppClient.
You can find detailed information about uuAppClient in [app-client.md](mdc:docs/command/app-client.md).
The uuAppClient is a client for the uuApp server. It provides a way to call commands of other subApps and process the results.

Since the API of other subApps can vary, you must follow these rules when implementing any steps that are calling
any commands.

- ALWAYS make sure that the base uri and use case is known and specified by the user.
- ALWAYS make sure that you understand what dtoIn will be used to call the command.
- ALWAYS make sure that you understand what is the dtoOut of the command.
- ALWAYS use the session of the current user, there is no way to get a session of another user in uuScript.
    This rule has precedence over the generic rule of AppClient for commands.

The uuAppClient can be used to call any HTTP endpoint, but it is mainly used to call uuCommands on uuSubApplications.
Whenever you need to call a uuCommand, you must always use the uuUri module to build the correct URL.
Never concatenate the URL manually, because it can lead to errors in the URL format.
For the documentation of uuUri, see [uri.md](mdc:docs/command/uri.md).

## 5. Implementation Guidelines

Always follow general rules, including the separation of competencies and responsibilities to different classes or helpers.

In uuScripts, you will be forced to use uuScriptRequire for importing helpers, which is a bit different from the
standard import. The uuScriptRequire is a function that loads the script dynamically and executes it in the context of the
uuScriptEngine. You can read more information about it in [script-require.md](mdc:docs/script/script-require.md).

Any script input data, session data, dtoOut with uuAppErrorMap or information about script runtime can be found in global variable
called scriptContext. This variable is available at the main script and all helpers loaded via uuScriptRequire.
See [script-context.md](mdc:docs/script/script-context.md) for more information about the scriptContext.

Always make sure that the generic-script-helper exists in the script library. If it does not exist, create it in
/src/helpers folder. ALWAYS name it generic-script-helper.js and if it does not exist, copy the content from
the example without any modifications!
It contains all the necessary functions that are shared between every script, such as validation,
error handling, and other helper functions. Check the [generic-script-helper.md](mdc:docs/script/generic-script-helper.md)
for more information about the generic-script-helper and how to use it.

Always prefer to use uuUri to handle any URI-related tasks, such as parsing, validating, or constructing URIs.
See the documentation at [uri.md](mdc:docs/command/uri.md) for more information about uuUri, uuUriBuilder and how to use it.

## 6. Validation Process

Always validate the input data of the script. The validation must be done in the validateDtoIn section of the script.
You must always use the validateDtoIn function from the generic-script-helper to validate the input data.
All standard validation functions are already implemented, in the script you just need to provide standard validation
scheme and use the validateDtoIn function to validate the input data. Use the validation documentation available
at [validation.md](mdc:docs/command/validation.md) and
[validation-scheme.md](mdc:docs/command/validation-scheme.md) for more information about the validation schemes and
all available data types.

There can be possibly multiple requirements for validations, such as
- validating that an uri passed in dtoIn is valid and that it contains
-- in this case, always use the uuUri module to validate the uri and extract any parameters, see [uri.md](mdc:docs/command/uri.md)

## 7. Error Handling

Every script must handle errors. The errors must be handled in a manner very similar to uuCommands,
see [errors.md](mdc:docs/command/errors.md) and [generic-script-helper.md](mdc:docs/script/generic-script-helper.md).
There must be no unnamed errors thrown in the script, it must always be an instance of UseCaseError.

## 8. Testing

Every script must have a related test file, which is located in /tests directory. The test file must be named
`<script-name>.test.js` and must contain at least a basic form of test that does not mock anything, just runs the script
in prepared test environment.

Always follow the practices and examples from the [script-testing.md](mdc:docs/script/script-testing.md) documentation.

Always prepare the test file regardless whether the user has requested it or not. It is a good practice to have the test file ready
and for localhost development, it will be necesary anyway.
